XCD protection: nano-HOWTO

1) russian letters in filenames are highly undesirable! (but still possible :-)
2) cd into dir which must be protected, and run dir /s /b /a-d >list.txt -
   and open this file by editor
3) in list.txt - remove lines about files that are unwanted on disc
4) context search & replace: "-i " instead of constant part of path - on each
   line
5) replace "-i" by "-x" for files desired as mode2-form2; "-i" by "-f" -
   for files that remains unprotected
6) add line "-@" (for rr-list) (the most precious file on disc! all other
   files can be recovered, this file can't; so place it at he beginning
   of root directory e.g. the safest place on disc)
   add line "-r" (for rr-data) (after last protected file i.e. after last
   "-i" or "-x" line)
7) double check that list is sorted by directory - situation like this
   -i dir1\file1
   -i dir2\file2
   -i dir1file3
   is TERRIBLY UNWANTED and attempt to mount such image may cause BSOD!

8) run command
   rrenc -s . -@ list.txt -wi -o list.um2 <protection-size> <rrlist.rrt> <_recvr_\rrdata.rrd>

9) you can make the image:
   m2cdm -paramfile list.um2


